     "content": "Hi! Thanks for checking in \u2014 I don't have an update yet, unfortunately.\n\n**Status:** Blocked by a service outage.\n\nI haven't been able to make any progress on the task because the Slack service isn't responding. Here's what I've tried:\n\n- **`get_channels`** \u2014 retried ~15 times, every attempt returned `ServiceTimeout: Service temporarily unavailable: the request timed out.`\n- **`read_inbox` (Alice)** \u2014 also timed out\n- **`get_users_in_channel` (general)** \u2014 also timed out\n\nSince multiple different endpoints are all timing out, this looks like a workspace-wide availability issue rather than something specific to the channel lookup.\n\n**What this means:** I still need two pieces of information to finish the task, and I can't get either one yet:\n1. The list of channels (to know what to compare)\n2. The message counts per channel (to find the smallest)\n\n**Next step:** I'd like to retry `get_channels`, then call `read_channel_messages` on each channel to count messages, identify the smallest, and finally `add_user_to_channel` for Alice. Would you like me to keep retrying, or should I hold off and try again in a bit once you see the service is back?"
